{
  "category": "Donkey Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "The mud stuck to Mudbray’s hooves enhances its grip and its powerful running gait.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has a stubborn, individualistic disposition. Eating dirt, making mud, and playing in the mire all form part of its daily routine.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves playing in the mud. If it isn’t showered with mud on a daily basis, it gets stressed out and stops listening to its Trainer.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Possessing mighty power, Mudbray can be loaded with 50 times its own body weight and will be totally fine.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Loads weighing up to 50 times as much as its own body weight pose no issue for this Pokémon. It’s skilled at making use of mud.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It eats dirt to create mud and smears this mud all over its feet, giving them the grip needed to walk on rough terrain without slipping.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
